{"step_index":159,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:03:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T17:03:31+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T17:03:35+02:00\nThe search for \"\"Lower bounds for the total\" \"k-domination number of a graph\" arxiv\" returned the following summary:\nThe paper you are likely looking for is **\"Lower bounds for the total (distance) k-domination number of a graph\"** by **Randy Davila**, which was indexed on arXiv in June 2024 (arXiv:2406.08770)[1][2][3].\n\n### Overview of the Paper\n*   **Topic:** The paper explores the \"total distance $k$-domination number\" of a graph, denoted as $\\gamma_{t,k}(G)$[3]. A total distance $k$-dominating set is a set $S \\subseteq V(G)$ such that every vertex in the graph is within distance $k$ of some vertex in $S$ *other than itself*[3].\n*   **Key Contribution:** The author notes that while there are many results for standard distance domination, there has been a relative lack of well-known lower bounds for the *total* $k$-domination variant[4][5]. This work establishes several new lower bounds and demonstrates how existing lower bounds for the total domination number can be generalized to the total distance $k$-domination number[3].\n*   **Context:** This research falls under the field of Combinatorics (math.CO)[2][6].\n\nYou can find the paper on the arXiv repository under the identifier **arXiv:2406.08770**[2][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [arxiv.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGjqIBVPfZgjmfHS1LUAjLyJ7qLcn9kt9MEGcVTJkvxRHuYx2OYJ8DEm3jNKrhFtxGn9yl3mJQMZrT2bnNqw4_6lhtjfAHohN0NwdSrjEaE2cSKf2pT)\n[2] [arxiv.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF4kJjFomTrGKKi6ASSmtJ_i4-m9MG3sQpt5Z4RQq5HotE3ZZV7k8JicmJkAngnwMVmeQsC8vvYnpY1jG6L34RmBAPR23TAJ6sNj038rMfGmw_mcN1erOFukJQYvQGN0WpOAV7N64rbkJ_1J2XM0h8=)\n[3] [arxiv.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEwpH6uSKRed-e9IF23t